# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_uninstall_resurrection.py" "UNINSTALL/ERASE RESURRECTION GATE: PASS" "uninstall/erase resurrection + phantom-tenant + processing-pile (audit iter-4)" "uninstall/erase resurrection (audit iter-4 P1, SECURITY/privacy): a BACKGROUND per-repo writer (co-change populate/per-push, self_heal_main_graph, boot-reconcile) could RESURRECT a purged/erased tenant across installation.deleted -- the uninstall purge runs ACCOUNT-WIDE holding NO advisory lock while the writer holds a PER-REPO lock (the lock-key asymmetry, so they do NOT serialize), so an in-flight task calls enter_installation_with_authority (which LAZILY RE-CREATED the deleted account) and writes co_change file PATHS / re-ingests the graph back into the resurrected tenant -- a GDPR/uninstall purge silently undone. THE FIX, proven here against a REAL DB: (a) purge + erase record a TOMBSTONE (core.account_lifecycle_tombstone) that SURVIVES the lifecycle event including erase (which hard-deletes the account row itself, so a deleted_at column could not survive -- a separate cross-tenant table written only via SECURITY DEFINER authority fns, REVOKE-from-PUBLIC, does); (b) enter_installation_with_authority REFUSES to lazily re-provision a tombstoned ERASED account (proven: account+installation rows stay 0); (c) the per-repo writers call core.assert_account_live_with_authority() AFTER lock/pin and BEFORE writing, which RAISES 42501 on a tombstone -- LOAD-BEARING for the PURGE case (the account row still EXISTS, so RLS alone would NOT block the write: a control write that bypasses the guard DOES resurrect data, the guard refuses it); (d) a GENUINE reinstall clears the tombstone via core.reactivate_account_with_authority() so a real reinstall WORKS (history preserved -- a post-reinstall write lands). STRUCTURAL recall-safety: each named background writer is asserted to CALL the guard (a refactor that drops it FAILS the gate). PLUS audit iter-4 P2 phantom-tenant: _event_account_key DROPS the installation.id fallback (a DIFFERENT id space that minted a split-brain phantom ACCT-GH-install_id) -- an install-id-only payload now resolves None (honest-unknown), while owner.id / installation.account.id / organization.id still key the real ACCT-GH-owner_id. PLUS audit iter-4 P2 observability: evaluate_delivery_depth gains delivery_processing_stuck -- a claim-then-crash loop piling 'processing' rows (re-picked only after the 1800s stale-reclaim) now PAGES, edge-triggered on processing>=N SUSTAINED over MORE THAN ONE tick (a single in-flight tick never false-pages) and resolving on drain. content-free + FORCE-RLS + least-privilege throughout" "uninstall/erase resurrection + phantom-tenant + processing-pile (audit iter-4): a background per-repo writer can no longer resurrect a purged/erased tenant across installation.deleted (tombstone + enter_installation refusal + a per-repo assert_account_live guard that is load-bearing for the retained-account purge case, with a genuine reinstall reactivating cleanly); _event_account_key no longer mints a phantom tenant from an install id; the durable inbox now pages on a sustained stuck-processing pile" 28
